msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:15
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"Show this once the Beta milestone is complete!\n"
"\n"
"Introducing **KDE Linux**, a free and open-source operating system built by "
"KDE that can turbocharge new computers and breathe life into old ones.\n"
"\n"
"KDE Linux is designed for general use, including the best implementation of "
"everything KDE has to offer, with the most advanced technologies.-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:22
msgid "**Help KDE build the next big thing!**"
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:24
msgid ""
"**KDE Linux** is a free, open-source, user-focused operating system being "
"built by KDE to include the best implementation of everything KDE has to "
"offer, using the most advanced technologies. Learn more on [the project’s "
"README](https://invent.kde.org/kde-linux/kde-linux#kde-linux)."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:28
msgid ""
"Designed to be safe, maintainable, functional, and modern, KDE Linux will be "
"the best choice for home use, enterprise workstations, public institutions, "
"pre-installation on computers you can buy, and more."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:30
msgid ""
"…Eventually! We’re not there yet, and need your help to make this goal a "
"reality."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:32
msgid ""
"{{< linux/button src=\"docs/install\" description=\"Install KDE Linux\" >}} "
"{{< linux/button src=\"docs/\" description=\"Read the docs\" >}}"
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:41
msgid ""
"<div class=\"help-section d-flex flex-row\">\n"
"  <div id=\"help\" class=\"w-50  g-0 p-0\">\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:44
msgid "How you can help"
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:45
msgid "You can help participate in the KDE Linux project in many ways:"
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:47
msgid ""
"**Help KDE Linux reach a wider audience**, especially if you’re a tech "
"journalist or other influencer. The more people know about KDE Linux, the "
"more chance the project has of receiving the love it needs to succeed."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:48
msgid ""
"**Daily-drive KDE Linux** or put it on a secondary machine, especially if "
"you’re a developer or adventurous power user. [Follow the installation "
"instructions](docs/install) to the letter; finding mistakes in the "
"installation process and discrepancies in the documentation is also "
"important."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:49
msgid ""
"**Test less-common hardware**, especially [NVIDIA GPUs](https://invent.kde."
"org/kde-linux/kde-linux/-/issues/281) and [using the experimental delta "
"update feature on spinning hard disks](https://invent.kde.org/kde-linux/kde-"
"linux/-/issues/280). Other testing on less-common hardware is also "
"appreciated."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:50
msgid ""
"**Report bugs**: issues with KDE Linux itself (initial system setup, device "
"compatibility, integration between components, etc.) should be reported on "
"[invent.kde.org](https://invent.kde.org/kde-linux/kde-linux/-/issues/). "
"Issues in KDE software — especially the experience of using it in a Flatpak "
"— should be reported on [bugs.kde.org](https://bugs.kde.org/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:51
msgid ""
"**Help develop KDE Linux**, especially if you have an interest in operating "
"systems (particularly image-based ones). There’s lots to do. [Chat with the "
"devs](https://matrix.to/#/%23kde-linux:kde.org) and [submit merge requests]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/kde-linux/kde-linux/-/merge_requests). If you’re "
"working on a similar OS, tell us about your experience, and we can compare "
"notes and work on solutions together. Shared knowledge improves all projects."
msgstr ""

#: content/_index.md:53
msgid ""
"</div>\n"
"<div id=\"help-image\" class=\"w-50 position-relative  g-0 p-0\">\n"
