msgid "Install Apps and Games"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/apps-and-games.md:11
msgid ""
"In KDE Linux, most software is packaged using a technology called [Flatpak]"
"(https://flatpak.org/) and distributed through https://flathub.org. You can "
"get this software in two ways: graphically using the _Discover_ software "
"center app, or using the <code>flatpak</code> command-line tool."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/apps-and-games.md:14 content/docs/cjkv-input.md:49
#: content/docs/updates.md:14
msgid "Graphical"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/apps-and-games.md:15
msgid ""
"_Discover_ is the primary tool for getting new software on KDE Linux. It’s "
"very easy to use; just launch it! You can use the search field to find "
"something specific, or browse through one of the categories in the sidebar "
"on the left side of the window."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/apps-and-games.md:17
msgid ""
"Discover includes productivity apps as well as games; many games are "
"available directly through Discover, plus emulators and game downloaders/"
