#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:0
msgid "Develop KDE Software That’s Shipped on the OS Image"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:13
msgid ""
"This workflow is used for developing KDE software that’s shipped on the base "
"system — or even Qt."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:15
msgid ""
"A list of such software [can be found here](https://invent.kde.org/kde-linux/"
"kde-linux-packages/-/blob/master/targets.yaml) (note that “workspace” "
"includes Plasma, KWin, and Plasma-aligned apps such as System Settings and "
"Discover)."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:17
msgid ""
"The best way to do this is by using <code>systemd-sysext</code>, which "
"allows overlaying built-from-source content on top of <code>/usr/</code> "
"without impacting the base system."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:21
msgid "Run the setup script:"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:23
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"set-up-system-development\n"
"</pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:29
msgid ""
"In a nutshell, you’ll compile and install software using <code>kde-builder</"
"code>, then refresh the systemd extension, and then finally restart any "
"services that you changed (e.g. Plasma), or the entire system."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:31
msgid ""
"For example, to compile and test a change to plasma-pa, do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:33
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"kde-builder plasma-pa\n"
"run0 systemd-sysext refresh --always-refresh=yes\n"
"systemctl restart --user plasma-plasmashell.service\n"
"</pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:39
msgid ""
"If you replace a core system component and find that everything is crashing "
"after the refresh is applied, try rebooting in order to fully reload the new "
"dependency in all running software."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:41
msgid ""
"When you’re finished developing or testing the change, disable (“un-merge”) "
"the system extension:"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:43 content/docs/override-usr.md:40
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"run0 systemd-sysext unmerge\n"
"</pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:47
msgid ""
"When you’re done with your built-from-source software (e.g. because it was "
"accepted as a patch and merged), delete the installed files:"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/kde-dev-host.md:49
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"rm -r ~/kde/usr/*\n"
"# When you’re prompted to delete the read-only extension-release.kde file, "
"answer 'n'\n"
"</pre>\n"
msgstr ""

