#: content/docs/nix.md:66
msgid ""
"The <code>nix \\<command\\></code> interface is still technically considered "
"[experimental](https://nix.dev/manual/nix/latest/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"profile.html) (more context on the “experimental” status of <code>nix "
"profile</code> can be found in [this RFC](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/"
"pull/136#discussion_r1123895460)), but in practice it’s widely-used, and "
"more ergonomic. Tab-completion and the <code>--help</code> options for the "
"various <code>nix</code> subcommands will also work out of the box on a "
"fresh installation. Like <code>nix-env</code>, <code>nix profile</code> will "
"install packages to <tt>/nix/store</tt> and make them available in your "
"search path, persisting between login sessions."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/nix.md:68
msgid ""
"Here’s a trivial example using <code>nix profile</code> to install the code "
"search tool [<code>ag</code>](https://github.com/ggreer/the_silver_searcher):"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/nix.md:70
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"$ mkdir -p ~/.config/nix\n"
"$ cat >> ~/.config/nix/nix.conf &lt;&lt;EOF\n"
"experimental-features = nix-command flakes\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"$ nix search nixpkgs silver searcher\n"
"⋮\n"
"* legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.silver-searcher (2.2.0)\n"
"  Code-searching tool similar to ack, but faster\n"
"\n"
"$ nix profile add nixpkgs#silver-searcher\n"
"$ which ag\n"
"/home/username/.nix-profile/bin/ag\n"
"</pre>\n"
msgstr ""

