"argument”, this is likely to be a [known issue](https://invent.kde.org/kde-"
"linux/kde-linux/-/issues/304) related to updates being advertised as "
"available before all update servers have fully synced."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/updates.md:35
msgid "Options for working around the issue include:"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/updates.md:36
msgid "Wait an hour or two."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/updates.md:37
msgid ""
"Set `KDE_LINUX_SYSUPDATED_ENABLE_STORE=1` somewhere in the environment (for "
"example in the `/etc/environment` file), and then restart."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/ventoy.md:0
msgid "Use Ventoy"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/ventoy.md:11
msgid "Ventoy is not supported for installing KDE Linux images:"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/ventoy.md:13
msgid ""
"**Technical limitations.** KDE Linux’s image-based boot process is "
"incompatible with Ventoy."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/ventoy.md:14
msgid ""
"**Questionable blobs.** Ventoy ships pre-built binary blobs not produced by "
"its own build system; concerns about this practice have been [raised "
"upstream](https://github.com/ventoy/Ventoy/issues/132) but [remain "
"unresolved](https://github.com/ventoy/Ventoy/issues/2795)."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/ventoy.md:15
msgid ""
"**Secure Boot bypass.** Ventoy is designed to [bypass Secure Boot](https://"
"www.ventoy.net/en/doc_secure.html) using a [reused Machine Owner Key]"
"(https://github.com/ventoy/Ventoy/issues/2184), which conflicts with KDE "
"Linux’s goals for code integrity verification."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/ventoy.md:17
msgid ""
"Please [create a live USB using the supported steps](install/#1-create-a-"
"live-usb-drive) instead."
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/virtual-cameras.md:0
msgid "Work with Virtual and Remote Cameras"
msgstr ""

#: content/docs/virtual-cameras.md:11
msgid ""
"It’s commonly believed that these workflows require the use of the out-of-"
"tree `v4l2loopback` kernel driver, but there are alternative methods that "
"work just as well. These methods work in KDE Linux, too; [read about them "
"here](https://www.ideasonboard.com/news/pipewire-is-the-new-v4l2loopback/)."
