msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:14
msgid ""
"Since KDE Linux is in an alpha stage of development, report every issue in "
"an eligible version that you encounter! Developers can then look into fixing "
"it for everyone, and advise you of any relevant workarounds in the meantime."
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:16
msgid ""
"Make sure the issue still happens in the latest version before reporting it "
"to the developers or requesting help from them."
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:18
msgid ""
"**To report issues in the KDE Linux operating system itself** (i.e. OS "
"design, integration, system services, etc), [use invent.kde.org](https://"
"invent.kde.org/kde-linux/kde-linux/-/work_items/new), and ignore the scary "
"red banner at the top of the page."
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:22
msgid "Support resources"
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:23
msgid ""
"KDE Linux is run by passionate volunteers who are eager to help with non-bug-"
"related issues you may encounter, but make no guarantees about their ability "
"to do so in a timely matter, to any level of success, or at all. All such "
"resources are provided on an “as available, best effort” basis."
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:25
msgid "Help is available in various forms:"
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:26
msgid ""
"**To get official answers to common questions**, [read the documentation](/"
"docs)."
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:27
msgid ""
"**To get help with a problem using KDE Linux**, [use discuss.kde.org]"
"(https://discuss.kde.org/), and tag your post with “kde-linux”."
msgstr ""

#: content/help.md:28
msgid ""
"**To talk with the KDE Linux developers about issues that may be bugs**, "
"[use Matrix](https://matrix.to/#/%23kde-linux:kde.org)."
msgstr ""

#: content/nvidia.md:0
msgid "The NVIDIA Situation"
msgstr ""

#: content/nvidia.md:10
msgid ""
"NVIDIA GPUs using an architecture older than Turing (this means anything "
"older than GTX 1630) require NVIDIA’s proprietary kernel modules. These "
"modules cannot be loaded at runtime because the base OS is image-based, and "
"pre-installing them appears to fall in a [legal gray area](https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel#Loadable_kernel_modules). To be safe, KDE "
"Linux doesn’t include them."
msgstr ""

#: content/nvidia.md:12
msgid ""
"Newer NVIDIA GPUs (Turing/GTX 1630 and newer) can use NVIDIA’s open kernel "
"modules which are redistributable with the base OS in a legally clear "
"manner, so KDE Linux pre-installs them. Necessary NVIDIA userspace drivers "
"and utilities are also pre-installed, so these GPUs should work without "
"drama."
msgstr ""

#: content/nvidia.md:14
msgid ""
"Older NVIDIA GPUs *should* work with the less-performant Nouveau drivers, "
"which are included. However support for this must be manually enabled right "
"now, and is not recommended for non-experts. Follow [the instructions](/docs/"
"pre-turing-nvidia), and temper your expectations accordingly."
msgstr ""

